0825f735ebf9fd3ea166d24465dbf0e49d24eeb87e3e8c","download_count":1,"created_at":"2026-09-09T13:10:27Z","updated_at":"2026-09-09T13:10:27Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/backbay-labs/chio/releases/download/v0.1.0/SHA256SUMS"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/backbay-labs/chio/tarball/v0.1.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/backbay-labs/chio/zipball/v0.1.0","body":"Chio CLI binaries for the existing `v0.1.0` source tag. These are the original release archives, published here on 2026-09-09 to restore public installer downloads. The binaries and their SHA-256 checksums are unchanged; this is not a new build from current main.\n\nInstall on macOS or Linux:\n\n```sh\ncurl -fsSL https://chio.computer/install.sh | sh\n```\n\nFor an installation into a writable directory without sudo:\n\n```sh\ncurl -fsSL https://chio.computer/install.sh | CHIO_INSTALL_DIR=\"$HOME/.local/bin\" CHIO_NO_SUDO=1 sh\n```\n\nArchives are available for macOS (Apple Silicon and Intel), Linux GNU (aarch64 and x86_64), and Windows x86_64. The shell installer supports macOS and Linux; Windows users can extract the ZIP directly.\n\nEach archive has a matching `.sha256` file. `SHA256SUMS` covers all five archives. After downloading the archives and checksum manifest into one directory:\n\n```sh\nshasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS\n```\n\nAll five archive checksums were verified during publication. The Apple Silicon macOS binary was also executed successfully with `--version` and `--help`, reporting `chio-cli 0.1.0`. Other target binaries were not executed in that verification.\n"}